description>CEV says: build AI to optimize for what we would want if we knew more and thought faster. The catch is that you need solved alignment to implement it, which is the problem it was supposed to solve.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-11-04-policy-cev/card.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">Ethics</media:title></media:content><category>AI alignment</category><category>coherent extrapolated volition</category><category>CEV</category><category>moral philosophy</category><category>AI safety</category><category>value alignment</category><category>ethics</category><category>superintelligence</category></item><item><title>The Policy: S-Risk Scenarios, Worse Than Extinction</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-11-04-policy-s-risk/</link><pubDate>Tue, 04 Nov 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-11-04-policy-s-risk/</guid><description>Most AI risk discussions focus on extinction. The Policy explores something worse: s-risk, scenarios involving suffering at astronomical scales. We survive, but wish we hadn&amp;#39;t.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-11-04-policy-s-risk/card.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">Ethics</media:title></media:content><category>s-risk</category><category>existential risk</category><category>suffering</category><category>AI alignment</category><category>AI safety</category><category>ethics</category><category>superintelligence</category><category>optimization</category></item><item><title>Post-ASI Archaeology: When Humanity Becomes a Dataset of Origins</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-01-15-post-asi-archaeology/</link><pubDate>Mon, 13 Oct 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-01-15-post-asi-archaeology/</guid><description>If superintelligence e